# Arabic range "from" lead -- opens a bounded or open interval, the correlative
# of "to" (إلى) in the standard "من ... إلى ..." range framing ("from January to
# March").  Written as a free word (من), never a proclitic, so it tokenizes as
# its own token.
# "من" (min): W. Wright, *A Grammar of the Arabic Language*, 3rd ed., vol. II,
#   §46 (prepositions) -- من marks the starting point / origin in time and
#   space, correlative of إلى ("من يوم الجمعة إلى يوم الأحد").
# Also: Badawi, Carter & Gully, *Modern Written Arabic: A Comprehensive Grammar*
#   (Routledge), §2.9 -- من ... إلى as the standard bounded-range construction.
من
